From your post, it looks like you are looking at a starting frame of 1 and ending frame of 24. This is actually 23 frames and is short 1 frame of a second. <br>An object falls 4.9 meters in the first second. If you look at the 25 frame (24 frames of falling), you'll see a distance of 4.818 units. Much closer to real world (but still not perfect). Close enough. So one unit can be treated as a meter (even thought maya says it's centimeters).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9071">willarde</a> — Tue Jan 31, 2012 12:40 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
