		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=26865#p26865"><![CDATA[
That's 9.8 metres per second <em class="text-italics">per second</em> - it's an acceleration. So after 1 second, your object should be travelling at 9.8m/s, but it won't have been at that velocity for the whole of the first second, and the distance travelled will be less than that. To get it to fall 9.8 metres in 1 second, you'll have to bump up the gravity, which is what you've found, and is correct.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7714">hymerman</a> — Sat Jan 28, 2012 7:02 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
